vin Marshall","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10419","person_slug":"gavin-marshall","vote":"no"},{"name":"Helen Kroger","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10712","person_slug":"helen-kroger","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ian Macdonald","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10401","person_slug":"ian-macdonald","vote":"no"},{"name":"Joe Ludwig","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10397","person_slug":"joe-ludwig","vote":"no"},{"name":"John Hogg","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10309","person_slug":"john-hogg","vote":"no"},{"name":"John Madigan","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10759","person_slug":"john-madigan","vote":"no"},{"name":"John Williams","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10716","person_slug":"john-williams","vote":"no"},{"name":"Judith Adams","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10005","person_slug":"judith-adams","vote":"no"},{"name":"Kate Lundy","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10398","person_slug":"kate-lundy","vote":"no"},{"name":"Larissa Waters","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10764","person_slug":"larissa-waters","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Lee Rhiannon","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10760","person_slug":"lee-rhiannon","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Lisa Singh","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10761","person_slug":"lisa-singh","vote":"no"},{"name":"Louise Pratt","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10714","person_slug":"louise-pratt","vote":"no"},{"name":"Marise Payne","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10509","person_slug":"marise-payne","vote":"no"},{"name":"Mark Furner","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10710","person_slug":"mark-furner","vote":"no"},{"name":"Mathias Cormann","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10148","person_slug":"mathias-cormann","vote":"no"},{"name":"Matt Thistlethwaite","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10762","person_slug":"matt-thistlethwaite","vote":"no"},{"name":"Michaelia Cash","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10707","person_slug":"michaelia-cash","vote":"no"},{"name":"Mitch Fifield","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10224","person_slug":"mitch-fifield","vote":"no"},{"name":"Nick Xenophon","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10717","person_slug":"nick-xenophon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Penny Wright","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10765","person_slug":"penny-wright","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Rachel Siewert","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Colbeck","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10131","person_slug":"richard-colbeck","vote":"no"},{"name":"Richard Di Natale","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10755","person_slug":"richard-di-natale","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Ron Boswell","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10057","person_slug":"ron-boswell","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ludlam","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10713","person_slug":"scott-ludlam","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Simon Birmingham","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10044","person_slug":"simon-birmingham","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Trish Crossin","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10161","person_slug":"trish-crossin","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ursula Stephens","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10609","person_slug":"ursula-stephens","vote":"no"}],"name":"Motions — Convoy of No Confidence","noes":37,"question":"Bob Brown I move: That— (a) the Senate requests Mr Alan Belford Jones AO apologise to the police and wider public for his false claim that thousands of people and hundreds of trucks, on their way to the 'Convoy of No Confidence' rally outside Parliament House on Monday, 22 August 2011, had been stopped at the border of New South Wales and the Australian Capital Territory; (b) the President report to the Senate on: (i) Mr Jones' claim that 'the people who have come here [Parliament House] can't actually get into the precinct to be heard', and (ii) whether people attending the rally were prevented in any way different to any other Australian coming to protest at Parliament House or whether this claim by Mr Jones is also false; and (c) Mr Jones be invited to respond to this motion, should it pass. Joe Ludwig Mr President, I think I am going to breach my own rule here. John Hogg Are you seeking leave? Joe Ludwig I am seeking leave, to make a very short statement. John Hogg Leave is granted for two minutes. Joe Ludwig Thank you. The government does understand the concerns that this motion raises. The government will not be supporting the motion. The parlia­ment, of course, is no stranger to intolerant expressions of opinion about matters of state. Some are expressed during protests in parts of the country, some are expressed out the front of the chamber, and sometimes they are expressed in the chamber, unfortunately. We do not, as a rule, support demands for an apology from those who make wrongheaded claims when engaging in public protest, whether they be in other parts of the country or in the proximity of parliament. Secondly, in relation to the advice about arrangements for access to the parliamentary precinct, there are other ways that information can be sought. For those reasons, the government will not be supporting the motion. Question put: That the motion (Senator Bob Brown's) be agreed to. The Senate divided. [12:36] (The President—Senator the Hon. JJ Hogg) Ques","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-2056","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2011-08-25/3"}
